with 503 a set number of times.\n`WeatherClient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, making up to 3 attempts in total.\n\n- **Retry rule:** only HTTP 503 triggers a retry. Any other error, and any failure on the last attempt, is raised straight to the caller as before.\n- **Backoff:** the client waits `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds between tries, which with the default is 0.5s and then 1s. `backoff` is a new constructor argument with a default of `0.5`, so existing callers don't need to change.\n\nI checked it against a local HTTP server (with the backoff shortened to 0.01s):\n\n| Server behaviour | Requests made | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, then 200 | 3 | returns the JSON |\n| 503 three times | 3 | raises `HTTPError 503` |\n| 500 | 1 | raises `HTTPError 500`, no retry |\n\nI didn't add a test file because the repo doesn't have any tests yet.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 34798, "requests_cache_write": 177986, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9314456, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1725, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial30", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 118, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:58:58.486286+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 28.557, "t_checker_s": 2.532, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1739, "tokens_cache_read": 34798, "tokens_cache_write": 177986, "tokens_fresh": 1739,